load @term/seed/code/structure/manifold
  find manifold

# The 120-cell grid, the regular honeycomb {5, 3, 3, 4}, hyperbolic four-space built from 120-cell polytopes. It is the
# ceiling of the construction: hyperbolic regular honeycombs exist only up to dimension four (Euclidean's revenge, since
# flat space tiles regularly in every dimension but curved space runs out after four). The splitting method still works
# here, but the addressing language is no longer regular and neighbor-finding turns slow. The form carries the
# underlying hyperbolic manifold.
form cell-120-grid
  link space, like manifold
